WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.135
 Dave, Gabe, congratulations.

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:05.905
You've made it into the final
round of this competition.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.340
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.010
forges us to recreate an
iconic weapon from history--

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:13.613
the yatagan.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.617
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:18.951
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:19.685
 Good luck.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.355 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.658
DAVE: I've been assigned
to make a yatagan.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.593
I don't know how
to spell yatagan,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.695
but here I am making one.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.266
I've never made a
blade this long,

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:36.435
and I've never made one that
requires such an ornate handle.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:37.804
So I'm nervous.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.239
This is going to have to chop
through a pig, a thigh bone,

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:42.108
maybe try to cut
through Wil's biceps.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.075
I don't know.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:44.944
I'm going to make it to cut.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.979
I think I've got
the curve right.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.581
I think I'm sitting pretty.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.017
Gabe, my competitor, is
a very competent smith,

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.919
so hopefully I'll have
a blade that will stand

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:56.589 line:14%
up and equal or surpass his.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.125 line:8%
GABE: It is very important
to get the rough shape today.

00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:01.427
And if I do not get the rough
shape knocked out today,

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:05.564
then that'll throw the rest
of the four days way behind.

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:08.667
I don't have a power
hammer or a forging press,

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.137
so I have a lot of work ahead.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.839
This is my power
hammer right here.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.575
I think I'm the underdog.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.542
Dave's got the upper hand.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.578
He's been doing it
for a lot longer.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:19.545
It's his to lose, I think.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.780
And I hope I'm going
to come in there

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.181
and sneak and take it from him.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.916
I really like the shape.

00:01:23.982 --> 00:01:26.319 line:14%
Dave, you're going down, buddy.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:29.455 line:8%
DAVE: Today, the plan is
to make my mokume billet

00:01:29.521 --> 00:01:32.058
for the bolsters and
the ornamentation that

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:34.627
goes on the side of the blade.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:38.530
Mokume technique in Japanese
means "wood grain metal."

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.333
It's laminated nickel
silver and copper.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.069
And I'm squeezing them
together under high heat,

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.338
and they should bind.

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:46.773
I'm going to create
an interesting pattern

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.774
in the steel.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:48.574
All right.

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:50.110
That's for later.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.411
It's quite time-consuming,
but I think the end product

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:55.781
will be worth it,
assuming it takes.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.116
That's hot.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.486
Now I see if I've
got a viable billet.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:01.754
Yes.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.588
Not molten.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.056
Also a good sign.

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.492 line:14%
This better be worth it.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.427 line:8%
 One thing I'm concentrating
on the most today

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:10.997
is making sure
everything is symmetrical

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.765
and getting ready
for heat treating.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.267
Feeling a little nervous.

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.068
If I have some things out
of whack, then it'll pull.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.371
That's one way you
can cause warps,

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.806
but I'm praying and hoping
that's not an issue.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.810
[music playing]

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.282
Hmm.

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.217
She has developed.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.185
I have a nice warp.

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:35.555
I don't have time to
make another blade.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:39.725
I have to fix this warp or
I have no shot at winning.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.694
[groans]

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:45.097
I'm going to clamp the
blade in a position

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:47.400
so that the warp
is overcorrected,

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.203
and hopefully it'll fix
itself in the temper.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.439 line:8%
Otherwise, I have no idea
what I'm going to do.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.541 line:14%
DAVE: The mokume came out great.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:56.508
It was worth it.

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:57.977
And yesterday, I
quenched the blade,

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.545
and it came out
straight and hard.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.847
Today, I'll start working
on the ebony handle.

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.250
So that to that.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.353
I chose ebony because
it's really pretty wood.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.221
The material's a
little brittle, but I

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:10.789
think it should be just fine.

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:13.459
I'm not really sure if I got
this thing fitted properly.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.628
Gonna hope for the
best right now.

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:18.263
Success.

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:20.866
I would like the test
to be on a banana--

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.401
a nice, soft banana.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:25.838
But I suspect it's going
to be a giraffe or a fire

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.406
hydrant or a cuckoo clock.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.141
I don't know what they're
going to come up with.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.743
I hope it does well.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.546 line:14%
[music playing]

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:38.417 line:8%
GABE: I fixed the warp as
best as I possibly could.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:41.854
The goal for today is to
be dialed in on the handle.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.656
I'm going with this marble wood.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.924
It's already square.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:48.361
It's got some width so that
I can sculpt in the ears.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.266
We are all together.

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:56.969
This sword I have dubbed
"Dumbo" because it

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.405
looks like an elephant.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:02.675
Everything's come together
into something I'm proud of.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.478
Let's go whack
something, shall we?

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.247
That's a pretty clean cut.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.884
I'll call that a day.

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:14.319
 Bladesmiths, to see
what kind of lethal damage

00:04:14.419 --> 00:04:15.988
your weapon will do,
I'll take your yatagan

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:19.225
and deliver slashes and thrusts
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.159
Dave, you're first.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:20.927
Are you ready?

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:21.794
 Yes, sir.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.096
 Let's do this.

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.764
DAVE (VOICEOVER): I'm
so nervous right now,

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:29.201
and I'm just hoping my
blade will perform well.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:32.405
[music playing]

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:45.217
 He's got bowels
dropping out everywhere.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.420
 Let's talk about
your weapon, Dave.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.355
It follows the
feel of a yatagan.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.158
It's supposed to be
light and deadly.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.326
The edge you have
here is sharp, where

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:56.729
it's curved in to lacerate.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.864
Your yatagan will kill.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.166
 Thank you very much.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.834
 All right, Gabe, your turn.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:02.568
You ready?

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.803
 Go nuts, man.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.870
 Let's do this.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.505
GABE (VOICEOVER):
Dave's blade performed

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.907
seemingly really well.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.376
Guts falling out of the
thing and blood everywhere.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.545
So a little nerve-racking
knowing that it'll have

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:15.848
to at least measure up to that.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.451
[music playing]

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.595
 All right, Gabe.

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:31.230
It is so light.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.032
It really feels
like it's not there.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:34.400
It's almost scary.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:39.005
When I thrust, it penetrates
easily and slashes down.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:42.140
Overall, sir, your
blade will kill.

00:05:42.207 --> 00:05:43.542
 Thank you.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.244
DAVE (VOICEOVER): I think
we cut quite similarly.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.580
I would prefer to be
ahead, but right now I

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:49.047
feel like we're neck and neck.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:50.216
 All right, gentlemen.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.284
This is the strength test.

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:53.852
To test the strength
of your weapon,

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:57.356
I'll be chopping into
these bones six times.

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:58.958
Dave, you're up first.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:01.260
 Hacking bone is
a very difficult

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.562
thing to do with a thin edge.

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:07.299
I'm aghast knowing what's
going to be coming.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.570
[music playing]

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.515
 All right, David.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.049
That's a tough test.

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:27.687
Those are very thick bones, but
what we've got going on here

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:31.023
is a lot of chipping and
distortion on your blade.

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:35.560
We've also got a major
crack in your handle that

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.930
runs right up through the pins.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:39.898
All right, Gabe.

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:40.533
Your turn.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.300
You ready for this?

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.335
 Go nuts.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:46.072
[music playing]

00:06:56.348 --> 00:06:58.084
 OK, Gabe.

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:00.086
The convex edge
you've got on here

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:04.056
is pretty much the perfect
edge for a test like this--

00:07:04.122 --> 00:07:06.659
sharp and strong.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:12.131
I can feel just the
smallest amount of a roll.

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:13.265
Nicely done.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:14.433
 Thank you.

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:15.467
 All right, gentlemen.

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.169
Next up, the sharpness test.

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:19.305
For that, I give you Doug.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:20.873
DAVE (VOICEOVER):
I have edge damage.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.408
I have handle damage.

00:07:22.474 --> 00:07:27.012
It's disheartening,
but it's not over yet.

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:30.249
 Bladesmiths, to see if
your blade is still sharp,

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:33.685
I will take your weapon and
slash through these silks.

00:07:33.785 --> 00:07:36.655
If your blade is still
sharp, it should cut cleanly.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:40.993
If not, it may rip or tear
or, worse, do nothing.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:41.760
Dave you're up first.

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:42.294
You ready?

00:07:42.394 --> 00:07:43.129
 Yes, sir.

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:43.930
 Let's do this.

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.602
[music playing]

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.810
 All right.

00:07:57.877 --> 00:08:00.379
I love the balance
of your blade.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:03.248
I like the way it
curves in, but you

00:08:03.348 --> 00:08:05.417
can really feel the edges now.

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:06.619
It's serrated.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.588
It hangs up with silk.

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:11.290
But then on the last piece,
just when it's nice and taut,

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.458
you can lacerate
and cut through it.

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:16.428
Overall, your blade
will still cut.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:17.329
 Thank you.

00:08:17.429 --> 00:08:18.296
 All right, Gabe.

00:08:18.363 --> 00:08:19.064
It's your turn.
You ready?

00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:19.765
 I'm ready.

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:22.168
 Let's do this.

00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:25.171
[music playing]

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:39.685
All right, Gabe.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:42.621
Your blade is so
light, you're barely

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:44.389
like cutting through air.

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:47.326
I glided through
this, lacerated,

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.562
and of course, in the
finishing cuts here,

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:52.230
cut easily through that silk.

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:53.899
It cuts.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:54.599
Good job.

00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:57.002
 Thank you very much.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:09:00.806
 Bladesmiths, you both created
remarkable finale weapons.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:02.575
But in this arena
of competition,

00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:05.377
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:07.078
and that champion is--

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:10.683
[music playing]

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:11.951
--Gabe.

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:14.953
Congratulations, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.790
Dave, your weapon
did not make the cut.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.692
 Dave, you brought us
an outstanding weapon.

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:21.327
That yatagan is fantastic.

00:09:21.393 --> 00:09:24.496
But during the strength test,
we lost structural integrity

00:09:24.596 --> 00:09:26.598
in the edge of your
blade and in the handle,

00:09:26.665 --> 00:09:28.167
with both scales fracturing.

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:29.868
And those are things we
obviously can't overlook,

00:09:29.968 --> 00:09:31.403
so that's why we're
going to let you go.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.604
 Sure.

00:09:32.704 --> 00:09:35.073
 Dave, please
surrender your weapon.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.743
DAVE (VOICEOVER): It's
exactly what I expected.

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:39.378
It was very difficult
testing, but I'm

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:43.482
still the guy with the cracked
edge and the broken handle.

00:09:43.548 --> 00:09:45.851
It's like going out
with a beautiful blonde

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:48.587
and finding out she has BO.

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:50.790
And my blade has BO.

00:09:53.725 --> 00:09:55.528
 Gabe, congratulations.

00:09:55.628 --> 00:09:56.962
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:09:57.028 --> 00:09:59.832
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:00.799
Good job.

00:10:00.866 --> 00:10:02.501
I've never seen
anybody less stoked

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:04.604
about getting 10 grand
in my entire life.

00:10:04.704 --> 00:10:07.373
Why don't you please present
that weapon to the judges.

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:09.542
GABE (VOICEOVER): It feels
great to be the "Forged in Fire"

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:11.276
champion, but I'll
do my celebrating

00:10:11.343 --> 00:10:12.845
behind closed doors.

00:10:12.911 --> 00:10:16.114
I felt like I was the underdog,
but underdogs win sometimes,

00:10:16.181 --> 00:10:16.882
I guess.

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:17.549
[laughs]

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.886
[music playing]

